In every training conducted in this subsection, two convergence criteria have been employed: the Total Loss Criterion and the Loss Plateau Criterion. For the Total Loss Criterion, the following equation is employed:
    \begin{equation}\label{eq14a}
          f^{crit}_{i} = |log_{10}(\mathcal{L}^{n}_i)-log_{10}(\mathcal{L}^{n-1000}_i)|
    \end{equation}
    where $i$ is the loss components and $n$ is current epoch.
For the Loss Plateau Criterion, we use the following equation (Eq. \ref{eq14b}) to halt training if the losses remain unchanged for a specified duration
    \begin{equation}\label{eq14b}
          Crit_{Plat} := \frac{\sum_i^{N_{comp}}{f^{crit}_i}}{N_{comp}}
    \end{equation}
By default, the model stops training when either the total loss drops below  $10^{-6}$ or $Crit_{Plat}\le10^{-4}$. If neither condition is met, training stops at the maximal epochs defined in Table.\ref{table3.1}.\par  
