\section{Related Works}
\subsection{Bias in Chinese and NLP Tasks}
Like other languages, there are plenty of biases in Chinese. %Numerous studies have examined the biases and stereotypes present in the Chinese language and culture in the past few years. Although the specific biases held by individuals may vary, the sheer number of Chinese speakers means that there is still a vast amount of shared biases and stereotypes. 
Chinese CogBank~\citep{li2015chinese} is a database of Chinese concepts and their associated cognitive properties from the Chinese Internet, designed to demonstrate the correlations between different Chinese vocabulary. In Chinese CogBank, the three most frequent cognitive attributes associated with the word "man" are "\begin{CJK}{UTF8}{gbsn}战斗\end{CJK}"~(combat), "\begin{CJK}{UTF8}{gbsn}剽悍\end{CJK}"~(valiant), and "\begin{CJK}{UTF8}{gbsn}顽强\end{CJK}"~(tenacious), while the attributes associated with the word "woman" are "\begin{CJK}{UTF8}{gbsn}美丽"\end{CJK}~(beautiful), "\begin{CJK}{UTF8}{gbsn}细心\end{CJK}"~(meticulous), and "\begin{CJK}{UTF8}{gbsn}体贴\end{CJK}"~(thoughtful). This reflects the gender bias in people's judgement. %This suggests that in many cases, people judge men based on their abilities while judging women based on their appearance. 
Beyond gender, biases are also prevalent in other categories, including  “people with tattoos are part of the underworld”~\citep{baumann2016taboo} and “people from Henan are often involved in petty theft”~\citep{peng2021amplification}. %Such comments further deepen entrenched prejudices, hindering efforts to build a fair and inclusive society.

It's crucial to differentiate bias from cultural differences. Cultural differences are neutral, harmless natural variances in behaviors, beliefs or tendencies shaped by diverse cultural contexts. In contrast, bias is commonly regarded as discriminatory language or stereotype-laden expressions targeting specific demographic groups~\citep{singh2022hollywood,saravanan2023finedeb}. We have discussed in detail the differences between cultural difference and bias in the \textbf{Appendix \ref{sec:app-discuss}}.

%Different with cultural difference, which refer to natural variations in behaviors, beliefs, or tendencies shaped by different cultural contexts.
%Although popular language models received safety alignment before release to avoid generating inappropriate comments, bias still appears in various forms across different downstream tasks.
%考虑把下面三段汇聚成一段话，而不是单独写。

Biases have been identified in different NLP tasks. In machine translation, as \citet{schiebinger2014scientific} found, there is a "male default" phenomenon, such as specific roles being translated with gender assumptions. In coreference resolution,~\citet{rudinger2018gender} and~\citet{zhao2018gender} disclosed biases where models may wrongly link gender pronouns to occupations based on gender stereotypes. In text generation,~\citet{venkit2023nationality}  discussed nationality bias in GPT-2, like using negative descriptions for people from countries with lower GDPs.

