\subsection{Generated Datapoint Filtering}
After the initial data generation, generated datapoints are then passed through the  filtering stage of the framework. 
Data filtration has been widely employed with the data augmentation discipline~\cite{soudani2024survey}. Many methods result in noisy, faulty data being included within the augmented datasets. A filtering step provides a way to ensure that any flawed datapoints are excluded. Whilst previous DA methods use filtering and relabeling steps, they primarily concentrate on class labels, frequently using a baseline classifier to obtain each generated datapoint's ``true label''. This approach is ineffective when the baseline classification performance is low, as is the case in this paper's tasks. 

