In summary, this paper presents a novel method to improve DIMT performance by using synchronously self-reviewing to preserve monolingual OCR proficiency while enabling cross-lingual DIMT. We demonstrate, through extensive experiments, that SSR significantly enhances the MLLM's generalization across both OCR and DIMT tasks, addressing challenges such as catastrophic forgetting and poor domain generalization.

