Our work differs from prior work in that we conducted our study in a non-lab setup with a collaborative task, while collecting results using both qualitative and quantitative measures. 
Unlike prior work which often examined animation and anthropomorphism in isolation, our study directly tests the interrelated functional impact of animation, anthropomorphism and icons on task performance and human perception using both objective and subjective metrics. 
