\section{Methodology}
We conducted a public space study to determine how display modalities could affect human robot communication in a shared navigation task.
Participants were volunteers who passed by our study setup.
In this task, both humans and the robot only had partial information, requiring effective communication for successful maze completion.
The public space setting ensured a valid environment for evaluating how non-verbal robotic displays affect communication in real-time and in the real world.  
