\section{Results}
% In this work, we systematically investigated 
In this work, we aimed to explore how different visual modalities would influence human-robot communication in a collaborative task. We set up a maze navigation experiment in a public setting with 37 non-expert volunteers. The robot was programmed with four distinct visual display modalities: animated eyes, animated icons, static eyes, and static icons. The volunteers were randomly assigned to one of two groups: Animated Displays or Static Displays. The human and the robot had to communicate with each other in order to complete the task. 

