\subsection{Participants with static eyes modality had the highest percentage of task successes to task failures}

We evaluated the performance of human participants in the maze navigation task with Cozmo across the four visual communication modalities: Static Eyes, Animated Eyes, Static Icons, and Animated Icons.  Performance was measured using the pass-to-fail ratio—the percentage of trials in which participants successfully reached the end of the maze out of the total number of attempts. 
% This metric was selected as a normalized indicator of task completion, allowing for direct comparison across modalities despite differences in the number of trials per group.
The pass-to-fail ratios for each modality are presented in \autoref{fig:suc}. Participants using the Static Eyes modality achieved the highest pass-to-fail ratio, successfully completing the maze in 70.59\% of trials. The Animated Eyes modality followed with a pass-to-fail ratio of 68.42\%. In comparison, the Static Icons modality resulted in a pass-to-fail ratio of 56.25\%, while the Animated Icons modality had the lowest pass-to-fail ratio at 50.00\%.

