\textbf{Summary of Maintained EC Modules.} 
There are 6 \textsc{Uncontrollable} module types without hyper-parameters grouped in Modular-EC:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item \textbf{\textsc{Initialization}}~\cite{initsurvey}, which initialize a population of solutions to kick start a EC optimizer. We have maintained 5 initialization variants in the low-level inheritance~(e.g., Sobol sampling~\cite{sobol}, LHS sampling~\cite{LHS}).
    \item \textbf{\textsc{Niching}}~\cite{multipop}, which divides the population into several sub-populations. We have maintained 3 niching variants in the low-level inheritance~(Random~\cite{dmspso}, Ranking~\cite{arruda2008pid} and Distance~\cite{liu2020niching}).
    \item \textbf{\textsc{Boundary\_Control}}~\cite{kadavy2023impact}, which ensures that the values of solutions in the population are all controlled in the bound. We have maintained 5 boundary control variants in the low-level inheritance~(e.g., Clip~\cite{kadavy2023impact}, Reflect~\cite{kadavy2023impact}).
    \item \textbf{\textsc{Selection}}~\cite{ga_selectsurvey}, which selects better solutions from parents/offsprings. We have maintained 6 variants of this type in the low-level inheritance~(e.g., DE-Crowding~\cite{jde21}, GA-Roulette~\cite{ga}).
    \item \textbf{\textsc{Restart\_Strategy}}~\cite{restartsurvey}, which re-initializes the population when it converges or stagnates. We have maintained 4 restart strategy variants in the low-level inheritance~(e.g., Stagnation~\cite{rJADE}, Obj\_Convergence~\cite{jde21}).
    \item \textbf{\textsc{Population\_Reduction}}~\cite{popsize_survey}, which reduces the population size to perform exploitative optimization. We have maintained 2 variants of this type in the low-level inheritance~(Linear~\cite{LSHADE} and Non-Linear~\cite{NL-SHADE-RSP}).
\end{enumerate}

