We set the eyeball rotation duration to 10 seconds, rotating around an axis parallel to the y-axis of the camera frame, from $-30^\circ$ to $+30^\circ$, resulting in a total of 300 frames for analysis. A tracking failure is defined as a deviation exceeding 30 pixels. Tab. \ref{tab:lost_frame} presents the number of frames in which each recognition method lost tracking out of the 300 frames. Cases where recognition was not possible are denoted by a "-" symbol. The frame loss statistics for each method are displayed in Tab. \ref{tab:lost_frame}.

